  "query_preview": "..\n\nKey Message 1...Periodic chances for showers and storms will \ncontinue, mainly for the western Southern Tier through tonight \nand expanding to western and north-central NY for Wednesday \nafternoon. \n\nGenerally northwest flow across much of the Great Lakes region with \nmultiple shortwaves passing under the broad scale troughing pattern \ncentered over the Hudson Bay. These shortwaves moving across the \nMidwest have brought continuous rounds of thunderstorms across \nIL/IN/OH, while a cold front looks to settle near the NY/PA border \nthis afternoon with widely scattered showers across the Southern \nTier. This placement will keep the majority of western and north-\ncentral NY dry through the remainder of the afternoon and evening. \n\nThe next approaching shortwave will pass through the lower Great \nLakes Wednesday afternoon bringing scattered showers and \nthunderstorms to the area. Instability will be fairly marginal \nhovering around 500-750 J/kg per the latest HREF/REFS for the \nwestern Southern Tier extending up to the Niagara Frontier. However, \nenough for a few strong thunderstorms to develop with 700mb flow \nincreasing to 30-35 kt in the afternoon. Heavy rainfall, lightning, \nand gusty winds would be the main hazards with these storms. \nInstability will be much less farther east towards the north \ncountry, but better synoptic lift ahead of the jet max may aid \nin additional shower and storm development in the vicinity of \nthe Tug Hill north into the St. Lawrence Valley through the\nearly evening.",
